QUENNE Prototype v1 Architecture

Goal: a working end-to-end demo where QUENNE’s layered intelligence controls a simulated ring segment (digital twin) with real APIs, measurable outputs, and auditability.

⸻

1) Prototype v1 Scope

What v1 proves
   •   Layered control loop works (sense → fuse → decide → act → verify → log)
   •   Strict neighbor-only layer communication
   •   Cross-platform runtime (Linux containers now; multi-ISA later)
   •   Safety + audit trail are not “future work”

What v1 does NOT try to prove
   •   Actual fusion / photonics / quantum hardware
   •   Full 10,000-person habitat
   •   Space-rated redundancy certification (that’s v2+)

⸻

2) System Topology (High Level)

Digital Twin (Sim)
   •   Ring Segment Simulator (100m–300m segment)
   •   Subsystems: power, thermal, air, water, mobility, structure, comms
   •   Fault injector + scenario runner

QUENNE Stack (Runtime)
   •   Layer 2–9 software instantiation (Layer 1 minimal)
   •   Each layer is a service with strict APIs (gRPC/Protobuf)
   •   Event bus for telemetry (Kafka/Redpanda optional) + real-time lane

Observability + Audit
   •   Metrics + traces (Prometheus + OpenTelemetry)
   •   Immutable event log (append-only ledger; simple hash-chain in v1)

⸻

3) Layer-by-Layer v1 Mapping (Practical)

Layer 1 — Cross-Platform Abstraction (Minimal in v1)

Role: unify device/sim interfaces
v1 implementation:
   •   quenne-hal-sim adapters: sensor API + actuator API
   •   “Board Support Package” becomes “Sim Support Package” (SSP)

Layer 2 — Linux Core (Real in v1)

Role: deterministic runtime, containerization
v1 implementation:
   •   Linux + containers (Docker/Podman)
   •   Optional: PREEMPT_RT kernel (nice-to-have for v1)
   •   Service supervisor: systemd

Layer 3 — Quantum Algorithm (Stub + Interface Real)

Role: quantum-inspired optimizer interface
v1 implementation:
   •   Provide a real API + a classical solver backend (MILP / evolutionary)
   •   Keep the “quantum provider” pluggable (future D-Wave / QPU)

Layer 4 — Engineering Algorithm (Real)

Role: digital twin + structural/ops optimization
v1 implementation:
   •   Model Predictive Control (MPC) for thermal/power/air loops
   •   Constraint solver for resource & safety budgets
   •   “Engineering Budget Enforcer” outputs safe setpoints

Layer 5 — Hybrid Photonic-Electronic (Emulated)

Role: ultra-low latency control + security augmentation
v1 implementation:
   •   “Fast lane” message path (gRPC low-latency channel)
   •   Crypto module with placeholder for QKD-derived keys
   •   Optional: simulated neuromorphic module (spiking toy model)

Layer 6 — Booster Fusion (Real)

Role: adaptive compute / energy scaling
v1 implementation:
   •   Resource scheduler service (CPU/GPU quotas, priority, backpressure)
   •   Predictive scaling based on scenario load + fault conditions

Layer 7 — Atomic Fusion (Real)

Role: multi-model cognitive fusion
v1 implementation:
   •   Sensor fusion (Kalman/particle + deep model optional)
   •   State estimator emits “Habitat State Vector” + uncertainty
   •   Data validation + anomaly scoring

Layer 8 — Nuclear Intelligence (Simulated Plant Controller)

Role: safety-critical energy control
v1 implementation:
   •   “Reactor Plant Simulator” (simplified) + SIL-style controller patterns
   •   Triple Modular Redundancy logic in software
   •   Interlock rules (hard constraints) + watchdogs

Layer 9 — Human Authority (Triad Governance Emulator)

Role: ethics + policy + override + audit
v1 implementation:
   •   Policy engine (rules + approvals)
   •   Two modes:
      •   Advisory mode: logs + recommendations
      •   Gatekeeper mode: must approve high-risk actions
   •   Produces signed decisions + rationale summaries

⸻

4) Core Data Flow (Control Loop)
	1.	Sensors (Sim) → Layer 1 adapter
	2.	Layer 7 fuses signals → StateVector
	3.	Layer 4 computes safe setpoints / constraints
	4.	Layer 6 allocates compute + prioritizes control tasks
	5.	Layer 8 enforces energy safety + interlocks
	6.	Layer 5 applies “fast lane + secure channel”
	7.	Actuators (Sim) execute (valves, radiators, power routing)
	8.	Layer 9 audits decisions + can veto/override
	9.	Everything is logged (hash-chained) + traced

⸻

5) Minimal v1 Subsystems (Choose 3 for a strong demo)

A) Energy + Thermal (most convincing)
   •   power demand forecasting
   •   thermal loop regulation
   •   fault: radiator loss, reactor derate, short circuit

B) Life Support (public-friendly)
   •   CO₂ scrubbers, O₂ generation
   •   fault: leak, sensor drift, stuck valve

C) Compute Infrastructure (tech credibility)
   •   workload scheduling
   •   degraded mode operation
   •   fault: node loss, network partition

