7) v1 Success Criteria (Measurable)

Your v1 demo is “real” when you can show:
   •   Stability: thermal/power remain within bounds for N hours sim-time
   •   Resilience: system recovers from injected faults (node loss, sensor drift)
   •   Governance: Layer 9 blocks risky actions (e.g., unsafe reactor ramp)
   •   Auditability: every decision has a trace + hash-chained log
   •   Reproducibility: scenarios run deterministically from a seed

⸻

8) The v1 Demo Everyone Understands

“Autonomous Ring Segment Survives a Crisis”
   •   start nominal operation
   •   inject cascading faults
   •   show QUENNE responding safely
   •   show governance veto once
   •   show recovery and a report output

That single demo converts skeptics into collaborators.
